where-inside-dump: `where` returns matches plus every definition. For `where leaf` case: `equals matches[].name` expected ["leaf"], but now there are many names → fail. Also `includes` still passes but `equals` fails → A5-specific-answer NOT MET. Also `ambiguous` expected false but matches.length > 1 → contract fails. And A5-default-text textIncludes still passes (leaf and chain/logic.ts:3 present somewhere in the dump!). Actually textIncludes would still pass because the dump contains leaf and its location. But A5-specific-answer (JSON) fails. So A5 marked NOT MET from one of two cases. Good.

